{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChainSafe/ssz/pulls/556","id":4889704333,"node_id":"PR_kwDODmwhAs8AAAABI3L3jQ","html_url":"https://github.com/ChainSafe/ssz/pull/556","diff_url":"https://github.com/ChainSafe/ssz/pull/556.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ChainSafe/ssz/pull/556.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChainSafe/ssz/issues/556","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChainSafe/ssz/pulls/556/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChainSafe/ssz/pulls/556/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChainSafe/ssz/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChainSafe/ssz/issues/556/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ChainSafe/ssz/statuses/8ac6df088d3b6964af0ce4f659838443caa865ba","number":556,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"chore: include end offset in arrayComposite offsets","user":{"login":"lodekeeper","id":258435968,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2drgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258435968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper","html_url":"https://github.com/lodekeeper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Motivation**\n\n`readOffsetsArrayComposite()` returned one offset per element, so both deserialize loops in `arrayComposite.ts` had to special case the last element (`i === length - 1 ? end : start + offsets[i + 1]`). The comments next to them (\"Capture length before pushing end offset\", \"offests include the last element end\") describe an n + 1 layout that the code no longer had.\n\nThis also lets #555 drop the `withEndOffset` flag it adds to `readVariableOffsetsArrayComposite()`, since that is the layout `SerializedList` needs.\n\n**Description**\n\n- `readVariableOffsetsArrayComposite()` and the fixed size branch of `readOffsetsArrayComposite()` now return n + 1 offsets, with a trailing entry equal to `end - start`. An empty array returns `[0]`\n- `assertValidArrayLength()` still gets the element count (`offsets.length - 1`)\n- `value_deserializeFromBytesArrayComposite()` and `tree_deserializeFromBytesArrayComposite()` use `endEl = start + offsets[i + 1]` with no branch\n\nBoth readers are module private and these two functions are their only callers. ProgressiveList has its own offset readers and is only affected through its use of `value_deserializeFromBytesArrayComposite()`. Validation and error order are unchanged. The trailing write happens after all offset checks.\n\nOne theoretical difference: the trailing entry is a `Uint32Array` value, so a serialized array of 2^32 bytes or more would wrap. The previous code used `end` for the last variable size element. That input is already invalid SSZ (offsets are 4 bytes), and the fixed size branch already wrapped for such sizes before this change.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `pnpm test:unit`: 1802 passed\n- `pnpm test:spec-generic`: 5065 passed\n- `pnpm test:spec-static-minimal`: 13284 passed, `pnpm test:spec-static-mainnet`: 540 passed\n- `pnpm lint` clean\n\n**Benchmarks**\n\nLocal, node 24 (V8 13.6), medians of interleaved master/branch runs (3 rounds for the large cases, 5 for the small ones), `deserialize()` = value and `deserializeToView()` = tree.\n\n| case | value master | value branch | tree master | tree branch |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| List[ByteList] 1 x 100B | 0.88 us | 0.89 us | 2.66 us | 2.72 us |\n| List[ByteList] 4 x 100B | 2.93 us | 2.83 us | 6.61 us | 6.80 us |\n| List[ByteList] 1000 x 1000B | 1.05 ms | 1.05 ms | 3.53 ms | 3.75 ms |\n| List[ByteList] 10000 x 100B | 8.18 ms | 8.49 ms | 19.94 ms | 20.47 ms |\n| List[ByteList] 100000 x 0B | 8.30 ms | 7.54 ms | 28.97 ms | 28.46 ms |\n| ProgressiveList[ProgressiveByteList] 10000 x 100B | 8.65 ms | 8.54 ms | - | - |\n| List[Container(fixed 40B)] 1 | 0.52 us | 0.50 us | 2.52 us | 2.63 us |\n| List[Container(fixed 40B)] 16 | 2.16 us | **2.89 us** | 6.21 us | 6.73 us |\n| List[Container(fixed 40B)] 128 | 14.03 us | 14.10 us | 36.83 us | 35.22 us |\n| List[Container(fixed 40B)] 100000 | 22.48 ms | 22.60 ms | 45.40 ms | 48.18 ms |\n| Vector[Bytes32, 4] | 0.57 us | 0.63 us | 0.93 us | 0.99 us |\n| Vector[Bytes32, 8192] | 0.42 ms | 0.43 ms | 0.95 ms | 0.93 ms |\n\nEverything is within run to run noise on this machine, except lists of exactly 16 elements. That case is consistent across all 5 rounds, about +0.4 to +0.7 us. V8 allocates typed arrays of up to 64 bytes on the JS heap. `Uint32Array(16)` is 64 bytes and costs about 33 ns, while `Uint32Array(17)` is 68 bytes, gets an off heap backing store and costs about 380 ns. So only n = 16 crosses the threshold. Lists of 15 or fewer stay on heap, and lists of 17 or more were already off heap. In practice this hits full 16 element lists such as `withdrawals` in every payload, about 0.5 us per deserialize.\n\nIf that matters, a follow-up could skip the offsets array for fixed size elements entirely (`start + i * fixedSize`). That would also remove the allocation master does today for fixed size lists.\n\n<details><summary>Bench file (not committed). The small cases used the same file with counts 1/4 (ByteList), 1/16/128 (Container) and Vector[Bytes32, 4]</summary>\n\n```ts\nimport {bench, describe} from \"@chainsafe/benchmark\";\nimport {\n  ByteListType,\n  ByteVectorType,\n  CompositeType,\n  ContainerType,\n  ListCompositeType,\n  ProgressiveByteListType,\n  ProgressiveListCompositeType,\n  UintNumberType,\n  VectorCompositeType,\n} from \"../../../src/index.ts\";\n\nconst bytes32 = new ByteVectorType(32);\nconst uint64 = new UintNumberType(8);\nconst byteList = new ByteListType(2 ** 30);\nconst fixedContainer = new ContainerType({root: bytes32, value: uint64}, {typeName: \"Container(fixed 40B)\"});\n\nfunction filledBytes(len: number, seed: number): Uint8Array {\n  const b = new Uint8Array(len);\n  for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) b[i] = (seed + i) & 0xff;\n  return b;\n}\n\nfunction byteLists(count: number, size: number): Uint8Array[] {\n  return Array.from({length: count}, (_, i) => filledBytes(size, i));\n}\n\ndescribe(\"arrayComposite deserialize\", () => {\n  const cases: {id: string; type: CompositeType<unknown, unknown, unknown>; value: unknown; tree: boolean}[] = [];\n\n  // variable size elements, readVariableOffsetsArrayComposite()\n  for (const [count, size] of [\n    [4, 100],\n    [1_000, 1_000],\n    [10_000, 100],\n    [100_000, 0],\n  ] as const) {\n    cases.push({\n      id: `List[ByteList] ${count} x ${size}B`,\n      type: new ListCompositeType(byteList, 2 ** 20),\n      value: byteLists(count, size),\n      tree: true,\n    });\n  }\n  cases.push({\n    id: \"ProgressiveList[ProgressiveByteList] 10000 x 100B\",\n    type: new ProgressiveListCompositeType(new ProgressiveByteListType()),\n    value: byteLists(10_000, 100),\n    tree: false,\n  });\n\n  // fixed size elements, fixed branch of readOffsetsArrayComposite()\n  for (const count of [16, 100_000]) {\n    cases.push({\n      id: `List[Container(fixed 40B)] ${count}`,\n      type: new ListCompositeType(fixedContainer, 2 ** 40),\n      value: Array.from({length: count}, (_, i) => ({root: filledBytes(32, i), value: i})),\n      tree: true,\n    });\n  }\n  cases.push({\n    id: \"Vector[Bytes32, 8192]\",\n    type: new VectorCompositeType(bytes32, 8192),\n    value: Array.from({length: 8192}, (_, i) => filledBytes(32, i)),\n    tree: true,\n  });\n\n  for (const {id, type, value, tree} of cases) {\n    const bytes = type.serialize(value);\n\n    bench({\n      id: `${id} - value`,\n      fn: () => {\n        type.deserialize(bytes);\n      },\n    });\n\n    if (tree) {\n      bench({\n        id: `${id} - tree`,\n        fn: () => {\n          type.deserializeToView(bytes);\n        },\n      });\n    }\n  }\n});\n```\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with AI assistance\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T14:20:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T14:26:21Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"081f6ce3417cc3651db7fa5cefda23d368f1e5df","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"lodekeeper:refactor/array-composite-end-offset","ref":"refactor/array-composite-end-offset","repo":{"id":1216804503,"node_id":"R_kgDOSIb2lw","name":"ssz","full_name":"lodekeeper/ssz","owner":{"login":"lodekeeper","id":258435968,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2drgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258435968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper","html_url":"https://github.com/lodekeeper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodekeeper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived"